# Explicit self-rewrites for every top-level static file in public/ that
# must NEVER fall through to the SPA shell — placed ABOVE the wildcard so
# there is no reliance on Cloudflare's implicit "exact static file wins over
# _redirects" priority (that assumption held under local `wrangler pages dev`
# but real-world reports showed a direct browser navigation to /sitemap.xml
# rendering the app shell instead of the file). _redirects rules are
# evaluated top-to-bottom, first match wins, so each of these claims its path
# before the catch-all ever sees it.
/sitemap.xml               /sitemap.xml               200
/robots.txt                /robots.txt                200
/favicon.svg               /favicon.svg               200
/manifest.webmanifest      /manifest.webmanifest      200
/manifest.hi.webmanifest   /manifest.hi.webmanifest   200
/og-default-en.png         /og-default-en.png         200
/og-default-hi.png         /og-default-hi.png         200
/offline.html              /offline.html              200
/assets/*                  /assets/:splat             200
/pwa/*                     /pwa/:splat                200
/marketing/*               /marketing/:splat          200

# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback — mirrors apps/web/vercel.json's rewrite rule.
# Vite copies public/* verbatim into dist/, so this ships as dist/_redirects.
# Cloudflare Pages serves an exact-match static file (e.g. the prerendered
# dist/en/index.html) BEFORE evaluating this rule, so /en and /hi still hit
# their prerendered snapshots, not this fallback — verified with
# `wrangler pages dev dist` (see docs/operations.md's Cloudflare Pages section).
#
# Destination is __spa-fallback.html, NOT index.html — confirmed live,
# 2026-07-26: Cloudflare's build-time redirect linter flags a literal
# "/* -> /index.html 200" as an "infinite loop" and silently DROPS the rule
# entirely (a false positive Cloudflare's own team has acknowledged:
# https://github.com/cloudflare/workers-sdk/issues/11824, but nothing
# repo-side can fix their linter). scripts/copy-spa-fallback.mjs copies
# dist/index.html to dist/__spa-fallback.html on every build specifically so
# this rule has a real, byte-identical, non-flagged target.
/*   /__spa-fallback.html   200
